{title: Those Three Days}
{st: Lucinda Williams}
{comment: Ukulele jam sheet | Standard G-C-E-A tuning}
{comment: Cmaj7 (0002) is an easy ukulele substitute for the chart's C/B transition}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]You say it's always [C]gonna be the same,
[G]Between us days are [C]filled with dreams,
[G]Scorpions crawl a[C]cross my screen,
[G]Make their home be[C]neath my skin,
[C]Underneath my dress they stick their tongues,
[G]Bite my flesh [C]down to the bone,
[G]And I have been so f**king a[D]lone,
Since those three days.

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Did you only [C]want me [Cmaj7]for those [D]three days?
[G]Did you only [C]need me [Cmaj7]for those [D]three days?
[G]Did you love me for[C]ever, [Cmaj7]just for those [D]three days?
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Turnaround}
[G]For those [C]three [Cmaj7]days [D]

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]You built a nest in[C]side my soul,
[G]You rest your head on [C]leaves of gold,
[G]You managed to crawl in[C]side my brain,
[G]You found a hole and [C]in you came,
[G]You sleep like a baby, [C]breathing in,
[G]Comfortable between [C]truth and pain,
[G]But the truth is nothings [D]been the same,
Since those three days.

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Did you only [C]want me [Cmaj7]for those [D]three days?
[G]Did you only [C]need me [Cmaj7]for those [D]three days?
[G]Did you love me for[C]ever, [Cmaj7]just for those [D]three days?
{end_of_chorus}
